ed-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 6]], "date-time": "2024-12-06T13:15:41Z", "timestamp": 1733490941000}, "score": 26.197235, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://neobiota.pensoft.net/article/129679/"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 6]]}, "references-count": 96, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.3897/neobiota.96.129679", "ISSN": ["1314-2488", "1619-0033"], "issn-type": [{"value": "1314-2488", "type": "electronic"}, {"value": "1619-0033", "type": "print"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 6]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 30]], "date-time": "2022-03-30T03:40:33Z", "timestamp": 1648611633923}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "American Library Association", "issue": "11", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Choice Reviews Online"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}, "DOI": "10.5860/choice.45-6282", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2013, 1, 24]], "date-time": "2013-01-24T08:27:05Z", "timestamp": 1359016025000}, "page": "45-6282-45-6282", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Rules to break and laws to follow: how your business can beat the crisis of short-termism"], "prefix": "10.5860", "volume": "45", "member": "3932", "container-title": ["Choice Reviews Online"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2016, 8, 11]], "date-time": "2016-08-11T19:13:54Z", "timestamp": 1470942834000}, "score": 24.430538, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://choicereviews.org/review/10.5860/CHOICE.45-6282"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}, "references-count": 0, "journal-issue": {"issue": "11", "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}}, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.5860/choice.45-6282", "ISSN": ["0009-4978", "1523-8253"], "issn-type": [{"value": "0009-4978", "type": "print"}, {"value": "1523-8253", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}}, {"institution": [{"name": "National Bureau of Economic Research", "acronym": ["NBER"], "place": ["Cambridge, MA"]}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 11]], "date-time": "2026-09-11T00:12:39Z", "timestamp": 1789085559713, "version": "build-2803163510"}, "publisher-location": "Cambridge, MA", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "National Bureau of Economic Research", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.3386/w13714", "type": "report", "created": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12, 28]], "date-time": "2007-12-28T14:18:41Z", "timestamp": 1198851521000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 4, "title": ["Do Professional Currency Managers Beat the Benchmark?"], "prefix": "10.3386", "author": [{"given": "Momtchil", "family": "Pojarliev", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Richard", "family": "Levich", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "1960", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12]]}, "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 10]], "date-time": "2026-09-10T23:59:50Z", "timestamp": 1789084790000}, "score": 23.918205, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.nber.org/papers/w13714.pdf"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.3386/w13714", "published": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 12]], "date-time": "2024-05-12T20:09:47Z", "timestamp": 1715544587532}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Cornell University Press", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9781501755644", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9781501755668", "type": "electronic"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 15]]}, "abstract": "<p>This chapter explicates the functions of rules in simulation. It elaborates on its two central functions in any classroom simulation: the rules tell students what they are allowed to do from class to class, and they tell students what they need to do in order to win the simulation. The chapter argues that simulations do not have to feature wars, but they do need competition and victory conditions. Competition and victory give purpose; they also drive student motivation. Ultimately, the chapter looks at the three examples, <italic>Greenwich Village</italic>, <italic>Galileo</italic>, <italic>Stages of Power</italic> \u2014 none of them featuring simulated armed conflict \u2014 and investigates how they use rules to inform and induce student activities. It then examines <italic>Great Power Rivalries</italic>, which does the same thing, but uses different rules for different students.</p>", "DOI": "10.7591/cornell/9781501755644.003.0004", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 20]], "date-time": "2022-01-20T14:35:12Z", "timestamp": 1642689312000}, "page": "56-70", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Rules"], "prefix": "10.7591", "author": [{"given": "Michael A.", "family": "Barnhart", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "4434", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 20]]}, "container-title": ["Can You Beat Churchill?"], "original-title": ["Rules"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 20]], "date-time": "2022-01-20T14:35:13Z", "timestamp": 1642689313000}, "score": 23.652632, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://cornell.universitypressscholarship.com/view/10.7591/cornell/9781501755644.001.0001/upso-9781501755644-chapter-004"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 15]]}, "ISBN": ["9781501755644", "9781501755668"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.7591/cornell/9781501755644.003.0004", "published": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 15]]}}], "items-per-page": 5, "query": {"start-index": 0, "search-terms": null}}}